course: dictionary
lesson: 12689
title: Divergent: going in different directions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Divergent means moving or spreading apart from one point, in different directions. Think of two paths that start at the same gate and then split apart. The word comes from the idea of diverging, which means going apart. «The two paths began at the same gate, but they soon became divergent.»
explain: The word also means different from each other, or different from what is usual. «The class had divergent views about the new playground rule» means the children did not agree. When you see divergent, ask: are things moving apart, or are they different from each other? The sentence will show you which.
explain: In thinking lessons, divergent thinking means coming up with many different ideas. «Try some divergent thinking: how many uses can you find for a brick?» Each answer should go in a different direction, not all the same.
fact: Divergent means moving or spreading apart in different directions from one point.
fact: «Divergent views» means people have different opinions and may disagree.
fact: «Divergent thinking» means coming up with many different ideas.
fact: In maths, a divergent series does not settle down to one value.
fact: In science, divergent plate boundaries are where Earth's plates move apart, and light rays from a lens can spread out in divergent directions.
exercise: «The two paths started at the same gate and became divergent.» What does divergent mean here? | Getting closer together | Very old | Muddy and slippery | *Moving apart in different directions
exercise: «The class had divergent views on the new rule.» What does divergent suggest? | Everyone agrees completely | *People have different opinions | The rule is about dogs | The class is very quiet
exercise: Mia says divergent thinking means finding one correct answer. What does divergent thinking really mean? | Finding the one right answer fast | Sitting quietly and waiting | Copying the answer from a friend | *Coming up with many different ideas
test: At a divergent plate boundary, what do Earth's plates do? | Crash into each other | *Move apart | Melt into one piece | Stay perfectly still
test: Which word means most nearly the same as divergent in «divergent views»? | Quiet | *Different | Shared | Identical
exam: «The light rays from the lens became divergent, spreading out from one point.» What does this show? | *The rays spread out in different directions | The rays come together at one point | The rays stop shining | The rays turn into sound
